At this juncture he has relied upon the decision reported in 2008 SCW 5261 in which he has held that;
Kumari Poonam vs Shri Gajendra C.V on 4 January, 2020 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/147021359/
4 Motor Vehicles Act, S.168---Accident--Claim for compensation--No material on record to show that wrong number of vehicle was noted by investigating officer---Thus on mere surmises and conjectures, no conclusion can be arrived at that investigating officer inadvertently mentioned wrong number of vehicle---Matter remanded for fresh consideration on merits.
